From: Facundo Arenas <facundoarenas29@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:31:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] D3D8 rendering for Rugby 08: fixed-function lighting,
 texture-stage combiner, pixel shaders, draw trace

- Vertex lighting as D3D does it: up to 8 directional/point/spot lights with attenuation,
  material colour sources, specular (D3DRS_SPECULARENABLE) added after the stages.
- General texture-stage combiner (D3DTOP 2-24, COMPLEMENT/ALPHAREPLICATE args); stage defaults per
  D3D (ARG2 = CURRENT). Stage 2 stays off for now.
- Pixel shaders: ps.1.x GLSL from MojoShader linked with the programmable or fixed-function vertex
  stage (varyings matched by io_<usage>_<index>), alpha test and fog injected, ps_tN inputs declared.
- DXT1 uploads as RGBA (punch-through alpha); texture address modes (MIRROR, CLAMP, BORDER).
- Draw trace (d3d9w_trace_draws): per-draw state, lights, stages, depth/stencil, textures and the
  framebuffer footprint of each draw.
